---
layout: article
title: Embed the video player
description: Embed the Appwrite video player on any website with an iframe. It streams adaptively, shows captions, and takes options for start time, autoplay, looping, controls, and accent color.
---

Every video comes with a hosted player, the same one you use in the Console. Embed it on any website with an `<iframe>`, or share its link, and viewers get adaptive streaming, captions, keyboard shortcuts, and picture in picture without you building a player.

To build playback into your own app with hls.js, Shaka Player, AVPlayer, ExoPlayer, or another player, see [Play a video in your app](/docs/products/videos/play).

# What viewers get {% #what-viewers-get %}

- **Adaptive streaming**: The player switches between your [renditions](/docs/products/videos/renditions) as the viewer's bandwidth changes. With HLS, it also caps quality at the player's size, so a small embed does not download 4K.
- **Captions and audio tracks**: Viewers pick a [caption](/docs/products/videos/captions) track and its size, and an audio track when the video has more than one.
- **Playback controls**: Playback speed from 0.5× to 2×, picture in picture, full screen, and a clock that switches between elapsed and remaining time when you click it.
- **Keyboard and touch**: [Keyboard shortcuts](#keyboard-shortcuts) on desktop, and [double tap to seek](#touch) on phones.
- **Media keys**: Media keys, the lock screen, and the system's now playing controls play, pause, and seek the video.
- **A responsive layout**: The controls size to the player, so a small embed or a phone keeps full screen and the settings menu.

# Before you start {% #before-you-start %}

1. Make sure the video has at least one `ready` [rendition](/docs/products/videos/renditions). Until then, the player shows **Not ready to play**.
2. To let anyone watch, turn on **Public playback** in the video's **Settings**. See [Who can watch](#who-can-watch).

# Embed a video {% #embed-a-video %}

1. Open **Videos** in your project and select a video.
2. Click **Embed**. Optionally, turn on **Custom start time** and set where playback begins.
3. Click **Copy embed code**, and paste it into your page:

```html
<iframe
  src="https://<CONSOLE_DOMAIN>/player/<VIDEO_ID>?project=<PROJECT_ID>"
  title="Product demo"
  allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture"
  allowfullscreen
  style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/9;border:0;"
></iframe>
```

The player is served from your Console's domain, at `/player/<VIDEO_ID>`. Keep the `allow` attribute: without it, browsers block autoplay, full screen, and picture in picture inside the frame.

The player fills the frame and fits the video inside it, with black bars when the shapes differ. Set `aspect-ratio` to match your video, such as `9/16` for a vertical clip.

To share the player as a link instead, open the URL from `src` on its own. It plays the same way.

# Preview and customize {% #preview-and-customize %}

Click **Preview** on a video to open the player live in a large panel, next to the [player options](#player-options). Changing an option updates the preview and the panel's **Query string**, and editing the query string updates the options.

When it looks right, click **Copy embed code** or **Copy URL**, or **Open in new tab** to try the player on its own. **Reset** sets every option back to its default.

# Player options {% #player-options %}

Add options to the player URL as query parameters. The player ignores a value it cannot read, so a typo never breaks the embed.

| Parameter | Default | What it does |
|-----------|---------|--------------|
| `project` | Required | Your project ID |
| `start` | `0` | Where playback begins. Takes seconds (`90`), units (`90s`, `1m30s`, `1h2m3s`), or a clock (`1:30`, `1:02:03`) |
| `autoplay` | Off | Plays as soon as the player loads. See [Autoplay](#autoplay) |
| `muted` | Off | Starts with the sound off |
| `loop` | Off | Plays again from the start when the video ends |
| `controls` | On | `controls=0` hides the control bar. Viewers click the picture to play or pause |
| `color` | White | Colors the progress bar and the volume. A hex color with 3 or 6 digits and no `#`, such as `fd366e` |

Turn a flag on with `1`, `true`, `yes`, `on`, or the bare parameter, such as `?loop`. Turn it off with `0`, `false`, `no`, or `off`.

For example, a silent product clip that loops from 12 seconds in, with a pink accent:

```text
https://<CONSOLE_DOMAIN>/player/<VIDEO_ID>?project=<PROJECT_ID>&start=12&autoplay=1&muted=1&loop=1&color=fd366e
```

## Autoplay {% #autoplay %}

Browsers often block autoplay with sound. When a browser refuses, the player starts the video muted instead and shows an **Unmute** button. To autoplay silently on purpose, such as a background clip, add `muted=1` as well.

Leave autoplay off for videos people choose to watch, and let them press play.

# Settings menu {% #settings-menu %}

The gear button in the control bar opens the player's settings:

| Setting | What it does |
|---------|--------------|
| **Quality** | **Auto** picks a rendition from bandwidth and player size, and shows the one playing. Pick a rendition to stay on it. Renditions of 720p and up show an **HD** badge, and 2160p and up a **4K** badge |
| **Playback speed** | 0.5× to 2× |
| **Subtitles** | Turns captions off, or picks a track. Shows when the video has captions |
| **Subtitle size** | Compact, standard, or large subtitles |
| **Audio** | Picks an audio track. Shows when the video has more than one |
| **Keyboard shortcuts** | Lists the [keyboard shortcuts](#keyboard-shortcuts). Shows on devices with a mouse or trackpad |
| **Stream format** | Switches between HLS, DASH, CMAF, and **Source**, the original file in Storage. A format with no ready rendition is turned off |
| **Inspector** | Opens the [inspector](/docs/products/videos/inspector) in a separate window, to check how the stream plays |
| **Reload stream** | Loads the stream again. A dot marks it when renditions finished after the player loaded |

The player starts on the first format with a ready rendition, in this order: HLS, CMAF, DASH. **Source** needs read access to the file in Storage.

Where the browser plays HLS on its own, as on some iPhones, the browser picks the quality and **Quality** does not show.

# Keyboard shortcuts {% #keyboard-shortcuts %}

Shortcuts work while the player has focus, so click an embedded player first. Press `?` to see the list in the player.

| Keys | Action |
|------|--------|
| `Space` or `K` | Play or pause |
| `←` `→` | Seek 5 seconds back or forward |
| `J` `L` | Seek 10 seconds back or forward |
| `,` `.` | Step one frame back or forward, while paused |
| `↑` `↓` | Change volume |
| `M` | Mute or unmute |
| `<` `>` | Change playback speed |
| `C` | Turn subtitles on or off |
| `F` | Full screen |
| `I` | Picture in picture |
| `0` to `9` | Jump to 0% to 90% of the video |
| `Home` `End` | Go to the start or end |
| `?` | Show keyboard shortcuts |

With a mouse, double-click the picture to enter or leave full screen.

# Touch {% #touch %}

On phones and tablets:

- Tap the picture to show the controls, and tap again to play or pause.
- Double tap the left or right side of the picture to seek 10 seconds back or forward. Each further tap seeks another 10 seconds.
- In full screen, a landscape video turns the phone to landscape.

# Who can watch {% #who-can-watch %}

The player follows the video's [permissions](/docs/products/videos/permissions):

- **Public videos** play for anyone. Turn on **Public playback** in the video's **Settings**, or grant **Read** to `Role.any()`. Visitors who are not signed in get the stream without scrubbing thumbnails, because they cannot read the video's [timeline](/docs/products/videos/timeline).
- **Private videos** play only for viewers signed in to the Console with an account that can read the video, such as members of your project. Everyone else sees **This video is private** and a **Sign in** button.

The player signs viewers in with an Appwrite Console account, not as users of your app. To show a private video to your app's users, build playback into your app as described in [Private playback](/docs/products/videos/permissions#private-playback).

# Troubleshooting {% #troubleshooting %}

| Message | Check |
|---------|-------|
| **Missing project** | The URL needs a `project` parameter, such as `?project=<PROJECT_ID>` |
| **Not ready to play** | No rendition is ready yet. Wait for encoding to finish, or [create a rendition](/docs/products/videos/renditions) |
| **This video is private** | Turn on **Public playback**, or sign in with an account that can read the video |
| **Access denied** | The signed-in account cannot read the video. Check the video's [permissions](/docs/products/videos/permissions) |
| **Video not found** | The video ID in the URL, and whether the video was deleted |
| Autoplay starts muted | The browser blocked sound. Viewers click **Unmute**. See [Autoplay](#autoplay) |
| Full screen or picture in picture does nothing | The iframe's `allow` attribute, and `allowfullscreen` |
| Shortcuts do nothing | Click the player first so it has focus |
| Stalls or low quality | Open **Inspector** from the settings menu to see buffer, bitrate, and network timing |
